#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:2
msgid "syncOwnership"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:6
msgid ""
"When enabled, Syncthing attempts to also synchronise ownership between "
"devices. Ownership is divided into two kinds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:9
msgid "\"Unix\" ownership, which is the Unix style UID and GID, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:10
msgid "\"Windows\" ownership, which the Windows file ownership concept."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:12
msgid ""
"The two are not mixed -- that is, ownership information is not synchronised "
"between POSIX and Windows systems, only POSIX-to-POSIX and Windows-to-"
"Windows. Nonetheless Syncthing attempts to leave unknown ownership data "
"intact: POSIX systems will not overwrite Windows ownership data but pass it "
"on unmodified, and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:19
msgid ""
"In order for there to be ownership information to apply, the peer device "
"must have either ``syncOwnership`` or :doc:`folder-send-ownership` enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:23
msgid "Unix implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:25
msgid ""
"Syncthing records both the numerical UID and GID for a file and the "
"corresponding user and group names, when they are known. When applying "
"ownership Syncthing will first attempt to look up a local user or group with "
"the given name, and if that fails it will fall back to the numerical UID and "
"GID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:32
msgid "Elevated permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:34
msgid ""
"Syncthing, when running as a normal user account, doesn't have permission to "
"alter file ownership. There are several reasonable ways of running Syncthing "
"with elevated permissions to enable ownership sync:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:38
msgid ""
"As root, in a Docker container, with the synced data mounted as a volume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:40
msgid "As a normal user, with extra capabilities granted to the executable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:42
msgid "To grant extra capabilities, the following steps must be taken:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:44
msgid "The executable must be owned by root and not writable by normal users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:45
msgid ""
"The executable must be granted the CHOWN and FOWNER capabilities. The CHOWN "
"capability is required to be able to change ownership on the file. However, "
"once that has been done Syncthing may no longer have permission to act on "
"the file in other ways while running as anonymous user. The FOWNER "
"capability overrides this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:51
msgid "Example commands of setting Syncthing up in this manner::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:53
msgid ""
"% sudo chown root /usr/local/bin/syncthing\n"
"% sudo chmod 755 /usr/local/bin/syncthing\n"
"% sudo setcap CAP_CHOWN,CAP_FOWNER=pe /usr/local/bin/syncthing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:57
msgid ""
"Note that automated upgrades cannot be used with Syncthing elevated in this "
"manner as any automated upgrade would undo the capabilities granted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:60
msgid ""
"When using systemd to start the service automatically, the capabilities can "
"be set in the unit file instead of touching the executable, see :ref:"
"`autostart-systemd-permissions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:65
msgid "Windows implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:67
msgid ""
"Syncthing records the account name of the owner, and whether it is a group "
"or user. On the receiving side a user or group with the corresponding name "
"is looked up and set as the owner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:71
msgid ""
"On Windows, syncing ownership has a fairly significant performance impact on "
"scan times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-sync-ownership.rst:74
msgid ":doc:`folder-send-ownership`"
msgstr ""
